      "adoption": "Historical incidents for non-China companies may proceed when contained and remediated; current unresolved issues remain held.",
      "usefulness": "Bitly user and group reads provide authenticated account inventory for link-management workflows without billed shorten writes.",
      "incident": "May 2014 Bitly disclosed unauthorized access to an offsite static backup after a compromised employee source-control account. Exposed data included email addresses, hashed passwords, API keys, and OAuth tokens for about 9.3 million users. Production was not reported compromised.",
      "remediation": "Bitly publicly disclosed, forced password resets, invalidated Facebook/Twitter credentials, rotated offsite-storage credentials, enabled 2FA on source-control accounts, and advised regenerating API keys. Vendor reported no confirmed follow-on account misuse. Bitly announced SOC 2 compliance in June 2025.",
      "residualRisk": "Historical 2014 backup exposure; customers who never rotated keys after 2014 remain theoretically exposed to that era's tokens. Live authentication and current security posture are unverified.",
